WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.540
Jerome Bruna's theory of development is
based on the assumption that we learn

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.730
best when we go from concrete to
abstract in a three-step process. First

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:18.029
comes hands-on action, then learning with
images, and finally students transform

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:22.800
what they've learned into language.
throughout the experience we constantly

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.630
revisit previously learned topics while
teachers provide carefully structured

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:33.719
guidance along the way. And it seems to
work.. In the 1980's the Singaporean

00:00:33.719 --> 00:00:39.270
government decided to stop importing
foreign textbooks and instead build the

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:42.270
world's best maths curriculum from
scratch.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:48.300
Since that time Singaporeans study fewer
concepts with greater detail following

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:53.070
Bruner's guideline. Before we learn how
well this worked out let's go through

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:58.670
each step of the theory with an example:
First, we learn through en-active

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:04.070
representation. This happens in hands-on
experiences ideally with real-world

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:10.260
applications: to divide 4 by 2, students learn to cut a cake into 4

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:16.340
slices so each can eat one now and bring
one home later.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:22.650
Step two is iconic representation: we now
link our memories of the experience to

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:27.600
iconic pictures. Students are asked to
draw a cake that was cut into four

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:33.450
pieces.
Last comes symbolic representation. We

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.920
now use the images we internalized
earlier and turn them into abstract

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:43.439
language such as mathematical symbols.
Using a little bit of retrospection we

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:47.210
can easily solve the problem.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.360
This last phase is also called language
based because we are really just

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:57.640
learning the right words and symbols to
express our thoughts. The actual maths

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:04.120
knowledge was acquired much earlier
through hands-on experiences. Bruner

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:08.560
therefore advocated for the use of a
spiral curriculum with continuous

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.950
repetition of the same fundamental ideas.
The curriculum is comprised of three

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:19.690
characteristics: students revisit the
same topic at regular intervals, the

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:24.700
complexity of the topic increases with
each revisit, the new learning has a

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:31.720
relationship with previous learning.
Teachers also use scaffolding, a term

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.880
coined by Bruner. Teachers do this by
structuring activities based on students

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.959
existing knowledge and in a way that
helps them to reach the desired learning

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:46.480
outcome. The teacher first demonstrates
the process as the student watches then

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.160
the teacher lets the students have a go,
steps back and offers support and

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:58.120
feedback when needed. Today, by the way,
Singapore's fourth and eighth graders

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:03.160
are the world's best in both mathematics
and science and Singapore's maths

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:10.209
curriculum is copied by educators from
around the world. Jerome Bruner was born

00:03:10.209 --> 00:03:16.780
blind in New York City in 1915. At the age of
two modern medicine restored his vision.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.790
Later he returned the favor by becoming
a pioneer in cognitive development.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:26.739
He believed that any subject can be
taught in an intellectually honest form,

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:34.030
to any child, at any stage of development.
What do you think about Bruna's theory

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:38.709
and his suggestion for better learning?
Is this how you learn in your studies? If

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:43.510
not, what is one subject that you think
could be made more understandable by

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.860
following his ideas?

